---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Fair Housing Commitment"
  description="Honest Acres Group's fair housing commitment: equal professional service for everyone, under the federal Fair Housing Act and the Texas Fair Housing Act."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Fair Housing Commitment</h1>

      <p class="eho">
        <span class="eho-mark" aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--green);">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="30" height="30" focusable="false">
            <path d="M12 3 L22 12 H19 V21 H14 V15 H10 V21 H5 V12 H2 Z" fill="currentColor" />
            <rect x="8.5" y="10.2" width="7" height="1.6" fill="#f7f2e7" />
            <rect x="8.5" y="13" width="7" height="1.6" fill="#f7f2e7" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span><strong>{SITE.fairHousing.slogan}</strong></span>
      </p>

      <p>{SITE.fairHousing.statement}</p>

      <h2>The law</h2>
      <p>
        The federal Fair Housing Act and the Texas Fair Housing Act
        (Texas Property Code, Chapter 301) prohibit discrimination in the
        sale or rental of housing, and in related services, because of:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Race</li>
        <li>Color</li>
        <li>Religion</li>
        <li>Sex</li>
        <li>Disability (handicap)</li>
        <li>Familial status</li>
        <li>National origin</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Texas Real Estate Commission rules (§531.19) likewise prohibit
        license holders from making or facilitating inquiries or disclosures
        that indicate any preference, limitation, or discrimination based on
        race, color, religion, sex, national origin, ancestry, familial
        status, or disability.
      </p>

      <h2>What that means in our marketing</h2>
      <p>
        We describe <em>property</em> — its land, water, soils, improvements,
        and location — not the people who might buy it. Our listings, guides,
        blog posts, and videos do not use language that states or implies a
        preference for or against any protected class, and we do not steer
        buyers toward or away from any area based on the people who live
        there. Everyone who contacts us receives the same honest service.
      </p>

      {SITE.agent.isRealtor && (
        <p>
          As a member of the National Association of REALTORS®, James also
          subscribes to its Code of Ethics, including Article 10's fair
          housing obligations.
        </p>
      )}

      <h2>If you believe your rights have been violated</h2>
      <p>
        You may file a fair housing complaint with the U.S. Department of
        Housing and Urban Development (HUD) — see
        <a href="https://www.hud.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">hud.gov</a> —
        or with the Texas Workforce Commission's Civil Rights Division,
        which enforces the Texas Fair Housing Act. You may also raise any
        concern directly with our broker,
        {' '}{SITE.brokerage.brokerName}, {SITE.brokerage.name}, at the
        address in this site's footer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
